Unix utility 'adduser'

The Unix utility 'adduser' interactively creates a new Hexagonix user account. It prompts
for a username, a password (entered twice, to confirm both match), a login shell and a
color theme, then stores the account as a new entry in the user database, alongside a
hash of the password, never the password itself. Only an administrative (root) user can
run it.

Leaving the shell or theme prompt blank falls back to a default (sh for the shell, dark
for the theme). Leaving the username blank, or entering one that already exists, or
typing two different passwords, aborts the operation with an explanatory message instead
of creating the account.

USAGE:

adduser

No additional parameters are required.

For more information, enter 'adduser ?' or 'adduser --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix Dormin development branch (2026).

